    "Gill Castle, a 44-year-old woman living with an ileostomy since 2011, developed a structured approach to overcome the challenges of swimming with a stoma. After years of leaks, she found success using convex bags, which offered better adhesion and security. She trained gradually in the North Sea, increasing exposure to tough conditions.\n\nOn September 12, 2023, Gill swam solo across the English Channel in 13 hours and 53 minutes, covering 21 nautical miles. Her stoma appliance remained perfectly sealed, proving it’s possible to swim at high levels with the right preparation.\n\n**Practical Tips for Swimming with a Stoma**\nUse high-adhesion convex pouches. Apply a barrier spray or protective film 30 minutes before entering water. Change the pouch no more than 2 hours before activity to ensure optimal adhesion. For extra security, use a stoma support belt, especially for long sessions. Always inspect the wafer seal and carry a spare kit.\n\n**Medical Guidelines and Cautions**\nWait at least 6–8 weeks post-surgery before swimming to allow full healing. Avoid highly chlorinated or dirty water that may irritate peristomal skin. Swimming is not advised during active skin infections, severe stenosis, or significant prolapse. Start with short 30-minute sessions, increasing gradually.\n\nA stoma is not a barrier to aquatic sports. With proper equipment, planning, and gradual reintroduction, swimming remains safe and empowering. Gill Castle’s example proves that strength is not the absence of change, but the courage to face it and swim through it." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Gill Castle, a 44-year-old woman living with an ileostomy since 2011, developed a structured approach to overcome the challenges of swimming with a stoma. After years of leaks, she found success using convex bags, which offered better adhesion and security. She trained gradually in the North Sea, increasing exposure to tough conditions.\n\nOn September 12, 2023, Gill swam solo across the English Channel in 13 hours and 53 minutes, covering 21 nautical miles. Her stoma appliance remained perfectly sealed, proving it’s possible to swim at high levels with the right preparation.\n\n**Practical Tips for Swimming with a Stoma**\nUse high-adhesion convex pouches. Apply a barrier spray or protective film 30 minutes before entering water. Change the pouch no more than 2 hours before activity to ensure optimal adhesion. For extra security, use a stoma support belt, especially for long sessions. Always inspect the wafer seal and carry a spare kit.\n\n**Medical Guidelines and Cautions**\nWait at least 6–8 weeks post-surgery before swimming to allow full healing. Avoid highly chlorinated or dirty water that may irritate peristomal skin. Swimming is not advised during active skin infections, severe stenosis, or significant prolapse. Start with short 30-minute sessions, increasing gradually.\n\nA stoma is not a barrier to aquatic sports. With proper equipment, planning, and gradual reintroduction, swimming remains safe and empowering. Gill Castle’s example proves that strength is not the absence of change, but the courage to face it and swim through it."
          }
        },
        "es-419" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Gill Castle, una mujer de 44 años que vive con ileostomía desde 2011, desarrolló un método organizado para superar los retos de nadar con un estoma. Después de años de fugas, encontró éxito usando bolsas convexas, que ofrecen mejor adhesión y seguridad. Se entrenó poco a poco en el Mar del Norte, aumentando su exposición a condiciones difíciles.\n\nEl 12 de septiembre de 2023, Gill nadó sola cruzando el Canal de la Mancha en 13 horas con 53 minutos, recorriendo 21 millas náuticas. Su sistema para estoma se mantuvo perfectamente sellado, demostrando que es posible nadar a alto nivel con la preparación adecuada.\n\n**Consejos prácticos para nadar con estoma**\nUsar bolsas convexas de alta adhesión. Aplicar un spray barrera o película protectora 30 minutos antes de meterte al agua. Cambiar la bolsa no más de 2 horas antes de la actividad para asegurar una mejor adhesión. Para mayor seguridad, usar un cinturón de soporte para estoma, especialmente en sesiones largas. Revisar siempre el sello de la placa y llevar un kit de repuesto.\n\n**Indicaciones médicas y precauciones**\nEsperar al menos de 6 a 8 semanas después de la cirugía antes de nadar para que la zona sane bien. Evitar aguas muy cloradas o sucias que puedan irritar la piel alrededor del estoma. No se recomienda nadar si tienes infecciones activas en la piel, estenosis severa o prolapsos importantes. Comienzar con sesiones cortas de 30 minutos e ir aumentando poco a poco.\n\nTener un estoma no es un obstáculo para los deportes acuáticos. Con el equipo correcto, una buena planeación y una reintroducción gradual, nadar es seguro y te puede empoderar. El ejemplo de Gill Castle nos muestra que la fuerza no es la ausencia de cambios, sino el valor para enfrentarlos y seguir adelante nadando."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Giuseppe Fama, Stomatherapist" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Giuseppe Fama, Stomatherapist"
          }
        },
        "es-419" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Giuseppe Fama, estomaterapeuta"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "If you've just received a stoma, the specialized clinic becomes your primary ally. Here you'll find specialized nurses who guide you step by step toward independence. You're not alone in this journey: these centers exist specifically to support you in transitioning to normal life.\n\n**When to Access the Service**\nYou can contact the clinic immediately after surgery, during the critical first month when the stoma changes shape and size, and for life whenever you need help. The service is open to all stoma patients, regardless of where you had your surgery.\n\n**What You'll Learn**\nDuring visits you'll learn daily management: perfect hygiene to keep skin healthy, when and how to change baseplates and pouches, which collection system suits you best. You'll learn to recognize and prevent problems like skin irritation, leaks from poor adhesion, stoma changes, and bowel blockages.\n\n**The Support Team**\nThe stoma care nurse will be your main reference, but you can also access a gastroenterologist for digestive problems, nutritionist to adapt your diet, psychologist for free emotional support, and oncologist if needed.\n\n**Warning Signs**\nContact the clinic immediately if the stoma becomes dark or black, you have severe continuous pain, haven't had a bowel movement for over 24 hours, have high fever with chills, or surrounding skin is very red and painful. Call within 24 hours for significant color changes, frequent leaks, persistent irritations, or urgent questions.\nThe stoma care clinic is your most important ally. Don't hesitate to use this service: it's made specifically for you and will help you discover that your stoma isn't an obstacle, but a solution to continue living life fully." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "If you've just received a stoma, the specialized clinic becomes your primary ally. Here you'll find specialized nurses who guide you step by step toward independence. You're not alone in this journey: these centers exist specifically to support you in transitioning to normal life.\n\n**When to Access the Service**\nYou can contact the clinic immediately after surgery, during the critical first month when the stoma changes shape and size, and for life whenever you need help. The service is open to all stoma patients, regardless of where you had your surgery.\n\n**What You'll Learn**\nDuring visits you'll learn daily management: perfect hygiene to keep skin healthy, when and how to change baseplates and pouches, which collection system suits you best. You'll learn to recognize and prevent problems like skin irritation, leaks from poor adhesion, stoma changes, and bowel blockages.\n\n**The Support Team**\nThe stoma care nurse will be your main reference, but you can also access a gastroenterologist for digestive problems, nutritionist to adapt your diet, psychologist for free emotional support, and oncologist if needed.\n\n**Warning Signs**\nContact the clinic immediately if the stoma becomes dark or black, you have severe continuous pain, haven't had a bowel movement for over 24 hours, have high fever with chills, or surrounding skin is very red and painful. Call within 24 hours for significant color changes, frequent leaks, persistent irritations, or urgent questions.\nThe stoma care clinic is your most important ally. Don't hesitate to use this service: it's made specifically for you and will help you discover that your stoma isn't an obstacle, but a solution to continue living life fully."
          }
        },
        "es-419" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Si acabas de recibir un estoma, la clínica especializada se convierte en su principal aliado. Aquí encontrarás enfermeras especializadas que te guiarán paso a paso hacia tu independencia. No estás solo en este proceso: estos centros existen específicamente para apoyarte en la transición a una vida normal.\n\n**Cuándo acceder al servicio**\nPuedes contactar con la clínica inmediatamente después de la cirugía, durante el primer mes crítico, cuando el estoma cambia de forma y tamaño, y de por vida siempre que necesites ayuda. El servicio está abierto a todos los pacientes con estoma, independientemente de dónde se haya realizado la cirugía.\n\n**Qué aprenderá**\nDurante las visitas, aprenderás sobre el manejo diario: higiene perfecta para mantener la piel sana, cuándo y cómo cambiar las placas base y las bolsas, y qué sistema de recolección es el más adecuado para ti. Aprenderás a reconocer y prevenir problemas como irritación de la piel, fugas por mala adhesión, cambios en el estoma y obstrucciones intestinales.\n\n**El Equipo de Apoyo**\nLa enfermera de estoma será tu principal referencia, pero también puedes acceder a un gastroenterólogo para problemas digestivos, un nutricionista para adaptar tu dieta, un psicólogo para apoyo emocional gratuito y un oncólogo si lo necesitas.\n\n**Señales de Alerta**\nContacta con la clínica inmediatamente si el estoma se oscurece o ennegrece, presenta dolor intenso y continuo, no has defecado en más de 24 horas, tienes fiebre alta con escalofríos o la piel circundante está muy enrojecida y adolorida. Llama dentro de las 24 horas si presentas cambios de color significativos, fugas frecuentes, irritaciones persistentes o preguntas urgentes.\nLa clínica de estoma es tu mejor aliado. No dudes en usar este servicio: está diseñado específicamente para ti y te ayudará a descubrir que tu estoma no es un obstáculo, sino una solución para seguir viviendo plenamente."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Ileostomy" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Ileostomy"
          }
        },
        "es-419" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Ileostomía"
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Ileostomia"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "ileostomy_description" : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "An ileostomy is a surgical opening constructed by bringing the end or loop of the small intestine (the ileum) out onto the surface of the skin. It allows waste to exit the body bypassing the colon."
          }
        },
        "es-419" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Una ileostomía es una abertura quirúrgica que se crea al llevar el extremo o un asa del intestino delgado (el íleon) hacia la superficie de la piel. Permite que los desechos salgan del cuerpo sin pasar por el colon."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Un'ileostomia è un'apertura chirurgica creata portando l'estremità o l'ansa dell'intestino tenue (ileo) sulla superficie della pelle. Permette ai rifiuti di uscire dal corpo bypassando il colon."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Important Notice" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Important Notice"
          }
        },
        "es-419" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Aviso Importante"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "In this section you will learn what a colostomy is, how it works and what aspects are important to know in daily life. \n\nA **colostomy** is a surgical opening on the abdomen, called a **stoma**, that allows feces to exit the colon to the outside of the body, where they are collected in a special adhesive bag. \n\nIt can be temporary or permanent, depending on the clinical condition. The feces no longer pass through the anus but through the stoma, into a bag. \n\nNow that you have a basic understanding, you're ready to begin. \n\n**Let's start this journey together!**" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "In this section you will learn what a colostomy is, how it works and what aspects are important to know in daily life. \n\nA **colostomy** is a surgical opening on the abdomen, called a **stoma**, that allows feces to exit the colon to the outside of the body, where they are collected in a special adhesive bag. \n\nIt can be temporary or permanent, depending on the clinical condition. The feces no longer pass through the anus but through the stoma, into a bag. \n\nNow that you have a basic understanding, you're ready to begin. \n\n**Let's start this journey together!**"
          }
        },
        "es-419" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "En esta sección aprenderá sobre qué es una colostomía, cómo funciona y qué aspectos son importantes para la vida diaria.\n\nUna **colostomía** es una abertura quirúrgica en el abdomen, llamada **estoma**, que permite que las heces salgan del colon al exterior del cuerpo, donde se recogen en una bolsa adhesiva especial.\n\nPuede ser temporal o permanente, según la condición clínica. Las heces ya no pasan por el ano, sino por el estoma, a una bolsa.\n\nAhora que tienes una comprensión básica, estás listo para comenzar.\n\n**¡Comencemos este viaje juntos!**"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "infoitem_adhesiveremover_description" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Gently lifts the wafer from the skin without pain or damage. Especially useful for sensitive skin or frequent pouch changes, this spray prevents trauma and makes removal easier and safer."
          }
        },
        "es-419" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Levanta suavemente la barrera adhesiva de la piel sin dolor o daño. Es especialmente útil para piel sensible o con cambios frecuentes de la bolsa, este spray previene el trauma y facilita una remoción más segura y fácil."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Solleva delicatamente la placca dalla pelle senza dolore o danni. Particolarmente utile per la pelle sensibile o per cambi frequenti della sacca, questo spray previene traumi e rende la rimozione più facile e sicura."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "infoitem_adhesiveremover_title" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Ostomy adhesive remover spray"
          }
        },
        "es-419" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Spray removedor de adhesivo para ostomía"
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Spray rimuovi-adesivo per stomia"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "infoitem_barrierring_description" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Flexible products that fill skin folds and help ensure a snug seal between the wafer and skin. They prevent leaks and protect the skin from irritation caused by output. Rings are pre-shaped; paste is moldable."
          }
        },
        "es-419" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Productos flexibles que rellenan los pliegues de la piel y ayudan a asegurar un sellado ajustado entre la barrera y la piel. Previenen fugas y protegen la piel de la irritación causada por las secreciones. Los anillos están preformados; la pasta es moldeable."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Prodotti flessibili che riempiono le pieghe della pelle e aiutano a garantire una tenuta aderente tra la placca e la pelle. Prevengono perdite e proteggono la pelle dall’irritazione causata dall’uscita. Gli anelli sono preformati; la pasta è modellabile."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "infoitem_barrierring_title" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Stoma paste"
          }
        },
        "es-419" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Pasta para estoma"
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Pasta per stomia"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "infoitem_onepiecebag_description" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "A device combining the adhesive barrier (wafer) and pouch in one. It collects waste from the stoma and can be emptied multiple times before changing. Ideal for frequent output, such as with ileostomies or colostomies."
          }
        },
        "es-419" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Dispositivo que combina la barrera adhesiva y la bolsa en uno solo. Recoge los desechos del estoma y puede vaciarse varias veces antes de cambiarlo. Ideal para salidas frecuentes, como en ileostomías o colostomías."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Dispositivo che combina barriera adesiva (placca) e sacca in un unico pezzo. Raccoglie i rifiuti dallo stoma e può essere svuotato più volte prima di essere cambiato. Ideale per uscite frequenti, come nelle ileostomie o colostomie."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "infoitem_onepiecebag_title" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "One-piece drainable ostomy pouch"
          }
        },
        "es-419" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Bolsa de ostomía drenable de una pieza"
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Sacca per stomia drenabile monopezzo"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "infoitem_scissors_description" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Used to cut the wafer to fit the exact size and shape of the stoma when pre-cut options are not suitable. The curved design ensures precise, safe cuts without damaging the protective layer."
          }
        },
        "es-419" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Se utiliza para cortar la barrera a la medida y forma exacta del estoma cuando las opciones pre-cortadas no son adecuadas. El diseño curvo asegura cortes precisos y seguros sin dañar la capa protectora."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Usato per tagliare la placca per adattarla alla misura e forma esatte dello stoma quando le opzioni pre-tagliate non sono adatte. Il design curvo garantisce tagli precisi e sicuri senza danneggiare lo strato protettivo."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "infoitem_scissors_title" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Curved scissors"
          }
        },
        "es-419" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Tijeras curvas"
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Forbici"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "infoitem_stomasizer_description" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "A stoma measuring plate or guide that helps to measure the size of a stoma."
          }
        },
        "es-419" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Una plantilla o guía para medir que ayuda a determinar el tamaño del estoma."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Una placca o guida per la misurazione della stomia che aiuta a determinare la dimensione della stomia."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "infoitem_stomasizer_title" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
